    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Celebrity couples who got married in 2020, showing that love really does triumph through almost anything\nauthor: KAELA MALIG; GMA News\ndate: 2020-12-23\n---\nCelebrity couples who got married in 2020, showing that love really does triumph through almost anything\n\nAlthough 2020 has given us some of the most unforgettable nightmares and grievances, it's also brought forth some of the most beautiful love stories told.\n\nDespite this year's hardships, 26 pairs of celebrity couples exchanged \"I do's\" and vowed their commitment amid such a trying time. They not only lent us the necessary kilig, but showed everybody that love really does triumph through almost anything.\n\n1. Megan Young and Mikael Daez\n\nMegan and Mikael's weddings and tear-jerking vows kickstarted the year right and made so many people believe in love again.\n\nThe couple, who have been together for more than eight years, tied the knot not just once, but twice, earlier in January.\n\nTheir first wedding ceremony was held in Batangas on Jan. 10, attended only by 10 guests. Meanwhile, their second wedding was held at San Roque Church in Subic on Jan. 25.\n\n2. Denden Lazaro and LA Revilla\n\nWho knew rivals could turn into life-long partners in real life?\n\nVolleyball star Denden Lazaro and basketball player LA Revilla tied the knot in January.\n\nThe two, who announced their engagement in January 2019, earlier played their respective sports for rival schools \u2014 Denden for Ateneo de Manila University and LA for De La Salle University.\n\n3. Joyce Pring and Juancho Trivino\n\nJoyce Pring and Juancho Trivino exchanged \"I do's\" on Feb. 9.\n\nThe couple, whose love story began on the set of GMA News' morning show \"Unang Hirit,\" where they were both hosts, tied the knot in an outdoor wedding ceremony at Sofitel Philippine Plaza.\n\nThe two got engaged in August 2019, but announced it only in November.\n\n4. Sheena Halili and Jeron Manzanero\n\nThey welcomed their first child, baby Martina, just this month, exactly nine months after actress Sheena Halili and non-showbiz boyfriend and lawyer Jeron Manzanero tied the knot in a beautiful Christian ceremony on Feb. 23.\n\nSheena and Jeron got married at The Blue Leaf Events Place in Que"
