    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 14 NFL Power Couples We're Rooting for This Season\nauthor: Lilly Blomquist\ndate: 2024-09-04\n---\nWhile NFL players have their natural talent, extreme discipline, and hours of training to thank for their performance on the football field, their significant others play a part in their thriving careers. Not only do these athletes' wives and girlfriends boost their morale by cheering them on from the stands, but they also offer emotional support behind the scenes, helping their partner cope with heartbreaking losses and nurse football-related injuries\u2014often in addition to juggling impressive careers of their own.\n\nThese professional athletes are more than the plays they run and the touchdowns they score on game day, though. Despite their jam-packed schedules, outside of the stadium, many of these football players prioritize nurturing their romantic relationships, whether they've been married with kids for years or they're exclusively dating. These couples go on date nights, such as grabbing dinner at a restaurant or attending red carpet events, and maintain private home lives, like cooking dinner together or playing with their kids.\n\nTo give you a glimpse inside of these football stars' personal lives, we've rounded up 14 of our favorite NFL couples. Read on to learn about their dreamy love stories.\n\nPatrick Mahomes and Brittany Matthews\n\nPatrick Mahomes might be a Super Bowl champion now, but his wife, Brittany Matthews, was right by his side back when the Kansas City Chiefs player was a high school quarterback in Texas. The two continued to date throughout high school and college, and once Mahomes was drafted to the NFL, Matthews was still beside him.\n\nAfter winning the Super Bowl in 2020, Mahomes proposed to Matthews at the Kansas City Chiefs' Ring Ceremony, so they both left the event with dazzling new bling. To top off their whirlwind year, the couple announced they were expecting a baby girl just a few weeks after their engagement, and they welcomed Sterling Skye in February 2021. The couple tied the knot in a romantic wedding in Hawaii on March 12, 2022, and that same year, Patrick \"Bronze\" Lavon was born. Now, the spouses are getting ready for another addition to their family.\n\nRussell Wilson and Ciara Wilson\n\nWhen Pittsburgh Steelers quarterback Russell Wilson and Grammy-winning artist Ciara Wilson first linked up in 2015, the world could hardly grasp how one couple could possess so much talent. Since making their public debut at a White House state dinner, Russell and Ciara have gone on"
  },
