    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Screen Rant\nauthor: Lynn Sharpe\ndate: 2023-11-27\n---\nSummary\n\n- Many Disney Channel actors have starred in multiple Disney Channel Original Movies (DCOMs).\n\n- There is a lot of actor overlap between DCOMs, with actors often appearing in different roles or guest-starring in other major franchises.\n\n- Some notable actors with multiple appearances in DCOMs include Raven-Symon\u00e9, Brenda Song, Corbin Bleu, Selena Gomez, Demi Lovato, and Dove Cameron.\n\nSeveral actors have starred in multiple Disney Channel TV shows, but many have also starred in multiple Disney Channel original movies. A Disney Channel Original Movie (DCOM) is a TV movie that was distributed/released by and originally aired on Disney Channel. For this reason, films like The Lizzie McGuire Movie and Hannah Montana: The Movie, despite being based on Disney Channel shows, aren't considered DCOMs, as they were originally released in theaters. The theatrical release rule also applies to High School Musical 3: Senior Year, which was released in theaters.\n\nRewatching Disney Channel Original Movies as an adult may not feel the same as they did as a kid, and while some Disney Channel Original Movies are much better than others, they still have major nostalgic appeal. There's also a lot of actor overlap between DCOMs. Of course, there are plenty of actors who have starred in multiple DCOMs from the same franchise. However, seeing an established Disney Channel actor starring in a completely different role or guest-appearing in another major franchise was always fun.\n\n12 Raven-Symon\u00e9 (7 Appearances)\n\nZenon: Girl of the 21st Century, Zenon: Z3, The Cheetah Girls, The Cheetah Girls 2: When In Spain, Kim Possible: A Sitch In Time, Kim Possible Movie: So The Drama\n\nRaven-Symon\u00e9 is best known for playing the lead role on the Disney Channel show, That's So Raven. However, before playing the titular psychic on That's So Raven (who was named after her), she starred in the DCOM, Zenon: Girl of the 21st Century (1999), as Nebula Wade. While she did not return for the sequel, Zenon: The Zequel in 2001, she did reprise her role in 2004's Zenon: Z3.\n\nRaven also played Galleria in DCOM, The Cheet"
