    "snippet": "---\ntitle: CBR\nauthor: Cameron Kelly\ndate: 2024-07-11\n---\nThe Disney Channel had a massive hold on children's pop culture from the early 2000s to the mid-2010s, with series and original movies gaining millions of viewers every week. The channel is best known for launching the careers of many well-known names in Hollywood and the music industry. Some of these names include Selena Gomez, Zendaya, Miley Cyrus and the Jonas Brothers.\n\nWhile many of these names were the leads of their respective Disney Channel series, many big names in Hollywood appeared on the channel in smaller roles in popular shows like Wizards of Waverly Place, Hannah Montana or The Suite Life of Zack and Cody. While some of these names appeared in guest starring roles before their big break, others were already well-known, whether for their work in television, film or music. Some of today's biggest Hollywood names appeared in these guest-starring roles on the channel.\n\n10 Tyra Banks Played an Awkward Librarian\n\nThe Model Guest Starred in Shake It Up Alongside Zendaya\n\n|\n\nSeries |\n\nShake it Up |\n\n|\n\nEpisode |\n\nSeason 2, Episode 16, Season 3, Episode 10 |\n\n|\n\nOriginal Air Date |\n\nMarch 25, 2012, February 24, 2013 |\n\nShake It Up follows the story of Rocky Blue and Cece Jones, teenage best friends living in Chicago who get cast in a live dance show. The series ran for three seasons from 2010 to 2013. Shake It Up is best known for launching the career of Zendaya, best known for roles as MJ in the MCU's Spider-Man trilogy, the Dune films, and Challengers.\n\nOne of the biggest guest stars of Shake It Up was Tyra Banks, the actress, model, and television producer best known for hosting the America's Next Top Model reality competition TV show. In the second season of Shake It Up, Banks had a cameo as Ms. Burke, the awkward and shy school librarian. In the third season episode, \"My Fair Librarian It Up,\" Banks reprised her role, with Rocky and Cece giving her a makeover to help her get a date with the poetry teacher, Mr. Zigfeld. (played by The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air actor Alfonso Ribeiro)\n\nShake It Up\n\n- Release Date\n\n- 2010 - 2012\n\nCast\n\n-\n\nBella ThorneCeCe Jones\n\n"
