    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 18 Celebrity Romances That Started on Set\nauthor: Boutayna Chokrane; Emma Specter\ndate: 2024-12-11\n---\nOff the top of your head, how many costars who dated can you name? Ariana Grande and her unexpected romance with Ethan Slater on the set of Wicked had the internet talking last year, and the rumor about Sydney Sweeney and her Anyone But You costar Glen Powell lingered for quite a while. Plus, we all finally received confirmation that The White Lotus's Meghann Fahy and Leo Woodall are, indeed, together.\n\nNow seemingly more than ever, costar romances are in the air\u2014which makes us think about some of the classic examples. Elizabeth Taylor and Richard Burton fell in love filming Cleopatra. Pen\u00e9lope Cruz is still going strong with Javier Bardem since working together on Vicky Cristina Barcelona, as are Games of Thrones stars Rose Leslie and Kit Harington. Below, take a trip down memory lane as we reminisce about more unforgettable costars who dated, both on and off screen.\n\nKeri Russell and Matthew Rhys\n\nSet: The Americans (2013)\n\nRelationship duration: The obvious chemistry between Russell and Rhys when they co-starred as married Soviet sleeper agents on The Americans wasn't only effective acting; the two started dating in 2014 (shortly after Russell's divorce from her first husband, Brooklyn-based contractor Shane Deary). Russell and Rhys are now co-parents to one son, in addition to Russell's two children from her first marriage.\n\nCurrent relationship status: Firmly partnered!\n\nFun fact: They've appeared on Watch What Happens with Andy Cohen together. (Bold for a straight couple!)\n\nHunter Schafer and Dominic Fike\n\nSet: Euphoria (2019)\n\nRelationship duration: This onetime couple met on the set of Euphoria and dated for more than a year before splitting up this past summer. As Schafer later told Alex Cooper on the Call Her Daddy podcast: \"It's one of the cleaner breakups I've had. We both recognized that this is not working, and we can't do this. We got to go our own separate ways. It was so, so hard because we really loved each other. He's a really special person and I love his soul and everything.\"\n\nCurrent relationship status: Broken up, but cordial.\n\nFun fact: Infidelity isn't easy for any couple to navigate, but it's nice to hear"
